From 25affcd98513fd08554fa8cd931348f236143909 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Boyd <danieljboyd@icloud.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 11:21:23 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] x11: type menus, tool tips, drag images and modal panels as
 GTK does

-setwindowlevel:: typed every window at the pop-up menu level other than
a tool tip as _NET_WM_WINDOW_TYPE_DIALOG, and modal panels as _NORMAL.
Window managers and compositors read the type to decide how to treat a
window, so menus and tool tips should say what they are.  Tool tips
were meant to be _TOOLTIP, but a tool tip's level is set while its window
is deferred, before the backend has registered the NSWindow for it, so
its class wasn't known and it was typed _DIALOG as well (libs-gui#965).

The typing moves to -_setWindowType:, which -setwindowlevel:: calls as
before and -orderwindow::: calls again just before mapping a window at
the pop-up menu level, when its class is known.  A tool tip is _TOOLTIP,
a menu panel at that level is _POPUP_MENU, a drag image (XGRawWindow or
GSRawWindow) is _DND, and a modal panel is _DIALOG, as GTK types them.
Each new type is followed by _DIALOG, the window's old type, so window
managers that don't know the new ones (Openbox 3.6 doesn't know _TOOLTIP
or _DND) treat the window as before.  Other windows keep their types, and
a theme can still set a finer type after the level (a menu bar's menus as
_DROPDOWN_MENU).

Testing: Tests/x11/windowtype.m forks a window manager that announces
itself as an EWMH one and maps what asks to be, then makes the windows
the gui makes, in the way it makes them (the tool tip deferred, its
level set before it has an X window), orders them in and reads back the
whole _NET_WM_WINDOW_TYPE list.  Comparing the whole list checks the
fallback type as well as the new one, and the tool tip case reproduces
the registration order that hid its class.  A plain window at the
pop-up menu level guards against typing other windows by level alone.
Without this change four of the five checks fail; with it all five
pass.  Under GNOME Shell 48.7 (X11), a real pop-up button menu, context
menu and tool tip were each typed _DIALOG without this change, and
_POPUP_MENU, _POPUP_MENU and _TOOLTIP (each followed by _DIALOG) with
it.  The test needs a display with no window manager of its own (a
private Xvfb) and skips otherwise.

AI assistance: this change, its test and this description were written
with Claude (Anthropic's Claude Code).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
